From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Santiago Hormazabal <santiagohssl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: don't dereference a missing PHY on port
 enable

User ports without a PHY, such as port 6 wired to an SFP cage through the
switch SerDes, get a NULL phy in .port_enable. Calling
phy_support_asym_pause() on it oopses as soon as the port is brought up:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 0000021c
  epc   : phy_copy_pause_bits+0x0/0x48
  ra    : qca8k_port_enable+0xf4/0x11c [qca8k]

Only advertise asymmetric pause when there is a PHY to configure.

Signed-off-by: Santiago Hormazabal <santiagohssl@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-common.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-common.c
@@ -784,7 +784,7 @@ int qca8k_port_enable(struct dsa_switch
 	qca8k_port_set_status(priv, port, 1);
 	priv->port_enabled_map |= BIT(port);
 
-	if (dsa_is_user_port(ds, port))
+	if (dsa_is_user_port(ds, port) && phy)
 		phy_support_asym_pause(phy);
 
 	return 0;
